  <title>4.9.3: Sketching Graphs of Functions</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01007</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.9.3: Sketching Graphs of Functions</md:title>
    <md:uuid>5b6f6843-7a1f-4499-9569-871c94147b1f</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <title>Activity</title>
      <para>Your teacher will show a video of a flag being raised. Function \(H\) gives the height of the flag over time. Height is measured in feet. Time is measured in seconds since the flag is fully secured to the string, which is when the video clip begins.</para>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated">
        <item>Use your own graph paper to sketch a graph that could represent the function \(H\). Be sure to include a label and a scale for each axis. 
    
    
    <para>Hint: <link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/c336085f25a08789727cb07e0502ac07b221d14f"/>Suggestion for how to set up graph</para>
 </item>
      </list>
      <example>
        <exercise>
          <problem>
            <para>Select the Solution button to compare your work, select the <emphasis>Solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Compare your answer:</para>
            <para>
              <figure>
                <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
                  <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_12_06_01.svg"/>
                </media>
              </figure>
           </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </example>
    </section>
  </content>
